==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Angry Delinquent Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Ultra Delinquent Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Delinquent Cat has high health, decent range and high DPS, along with the ability to freeze Floating enemies and a multi-hit to increase his activation chance. Adding onto this, because a lot of short-ranged bosses are [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]], Delinquent Cat is useful for a large number of early stages and, when decently leveled, he can take on many of the [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]], [[Teacher Bun Bun|Bun Bun]] and [[The Face|Face]] variants. However, his use drastically falls off after early-game, as [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] stacks replace him for DPS, while [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] or [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necro-Dancer Cat]] replace him as anti-Floating crowd-controllers due to their more reliable abilities, shorter cooldown and cheaper cost.

==='''True Form'''===
Although Ultra Delinquent Cat has higher range, curse immunity, more health and can additionally freeze [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] enemies, the usefulness of these abilities is questionable due to him still having all the faults of his previous form, which are his low chance to freeze and long recharge time preventing reliable stacking. Most Relics also outrange him, so he can only consistently freeze [[Oldhorn]], [[Relic Doge]], [[Sir Rel]] and the [[Primeval Cyclone]], or in stages where Floating enemies are backed by the [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]] and you must fight within range of it. You won't be using this True Form often, so it is recommended to prioritize spending your Elder [[Catfruit]] on more versatile units like [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]], [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]] and [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]].

However, when it comes to Floating-Relics mixed stages, he proves to be decently useful, an example of this kind of stage is [[Efficient Timewasting]], which has almost all Bun Bun variants, including [[Relic Bun-Bun]].

==='''Talents'''===
There isn't much to say about Ultra Delinquent Cat's Talents, for all do the same thing: make Delinquent a better generalist. If you do decide to invest in Ultra Delinquent Cat anyways, it is important to mention that at most, with Strengthen and Savage Blow, Ultra Delinquent Cat's DPS can reach up to 7,200, three times that of a typical Super Rare! Do keep in mind that his Savage Blow chance is only 10% at most. Multi-Hit does increase the activation chance of the Savage Blow significantly, but the chances are too low regardless for him to be effective. His relatively low survivability stays, along with the high cost and long cooldown, keeping him below the levels reachable by his competition, notably [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]], another Super Rare Crowd-Controlling generalist with Savage Blow as a Talent, who has a lower cooldown, higher standing (and piercing) range and overall more reliability. Overall, Ultra Delinquent Cat is not worth investing into as better generalists and crowd-controllers exist who can easily replace his niche.

==='''Orb'''===
Attack Up vs Floating or Attack Up vs Relics are the only viable orbs.

