==Trivia==
*[[Version 2.0 Update#Version 2.0.6 Update|Version 2.0.6]] increased Delinquent Cat's freeze chance from 10% to 40%.
*Prior to [[The Battle Cats|BCEN]] [[Version 3.6 Update|Version 3.6]], Delinquent Cat's name was misspelled as Deliquent Cat.
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Angry Delinquent Cat was a part of another [[Cat Combo]] called [[Shonen Manga (Removed Combo)|Shonen Manga]].
*He is one of the many Cats who were given [[Multi-Hit]] in [[Version 6.0 Update|Version 6.0]].
**The addition of Multi-Hit caused his Freeze chance to be reduced from 40% to 16%.
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Delinquent Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Delinquent Cat
Known as the Bancho of Cat School.
Might freeze Floating enemies (Area Attack)</pre>
<pre>Angry Delinquent Cat
Throwing a fit of rage because his dad
ate his ice cream that was in the fridge.
Might freeze Floating enemies (Area Attack)</pre>
<pre>Ultra Delinquent Cat
A naughty Cat known as king of the Angry Fist.
Loves pachinko, trades his winnings for ice cream.
Might freeze Floating/Relics (Area Attack)</pre>
*Delinquent Cat is a direct reference to [[jojowiki:Jotaro Kujo|Jotaro Kujo]] from ''[[wikipedia:JoJo's Bizarre Adventure|JoJo's Bizarre Adventure]]''.
**Jotaro debuted as a delinquent, and they both wear similar attire.
**His attack animation is identical to how Jotaro uses his Stand, [[jojowiki:Star Platinum|Star Platinum]].
**After the events of ''[[wikipedia:Stardust Crusaders|Stardust Crusaders]]'', Jotaro's Stand can stop time for 2 seconds, just like how Delinquent Cat can freeze [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating Enemies]] for 2 seconds.
**Also during ''Stardust Crusaders'', Jotaro Kujo was able to move in spite of his final opponent freezing time, which is referenced by Angry Delinquent Cat's immunity to Freeze.
**Delinquent Cat's updated description in [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]] also calls him ''bizarre'' and references Dio's Stand, [[jojowiki:The World|The World]].
*While Jotaro Kujo is undoubtedly the main inspiration for his design, Angry Delinquent Cat could also be a reference to Masami Iwaki from ''[[wikipedia:Dokaben|Dokaben]]'', whose typical look includes a student cap that meshes with his hair and a two-leaved twig in his mouth.
*Ultra Delinquent Cat's Japanese name, Osu! Neko Bancho (押忍！ネコ番長, "'Yes Sir!' Bancho Cat"), is a reference to to the pachislo machine series ''[[wikipedia:ja:押忍!番長|Osu! Bancho]]'' (押忍!番長). One of its characters, [https://dic.pixiv.net/a/轟金剛 Kongou Todoroki], is a Jotaro lookalike with long hair similar to that of Ultra Delinquent Cat's "Stand". Ultra Delinquent Cat's description even mentions pachinko in the Japanese Version.
*Ultra Delinquent Cat's English description mentions a "tough", meaning a rude and violent person, especially a gangster.
*The text that appears in Delinquent Cat's attack animation is にゃ and ニャ, the onomatopoeia ''nya'' (meow) written in hiragana and katakana respectively.
*The text that appears in Angry Delinquent Cat's attack animation is the kanji for rage, 怒, which in this context can be read as ''do'' or be short for 怒り ''ikari'' (anger), the first word in Angry Delinquent Cat's Japanese name.
*The text that appears in Ultra Delinquent Cat's attack animation is 押忍 ''osu'', which is used as an informal greeting between close male friends like "Yo!" or "Hey, man!" and as an interjection in martial arts contexts like "Yes, sir!" or "Understood!"
*Despite the Catfruit Evolution stating that the True Form increases all stats, it only increases range and health.
*In [[The Battle Cats POP!]], Angry Delinquent Cat is called Brawler Cat.

